File: \`SoulPilates.Services/InvoiceService.cs\` (paid-package provisioning, the \`product.IncludesFreePrivateClass\` block).
Before: bundled PRIVATE credit minted with \`FractionalValuePerClass = 0m\`.
After: \`FractionalValuePerClass = credits > 0 ? (perUnitTotal / credits) : 0m\` — the SAME per-class value the group credits from the same invoice line get (\`perUnitTotal = line.LineTotal / units\`).
Why it mattered: on redemption the PACKAGE_CREDIT commission path in \`PayrollService.ResolveAttendeeRevenueAsync\` guards \`FractionalValuePerClass > 0m\`; a 0 fell through to \`session.DropInPrice\` — paying the instructor the private DROP-IN rate for a free inclusion. Now it pays the group per-class rate.
Scope: only the paid-package site changed. Left untouched (correctly): \`WalletService.GrantPackageAsync\` (whole-package comp grant — group credits already 0, no paid value to derive; owner says a fully-free package won't happen); \`SchedulingService\`/\`PaymentService\` BOGO grants (unrelated free GROUP promo credits, not bundled free-private).

**(A) Split-bill / multi-package mis-attribution verdict — REACHABLE, split-bill does NOT prevent it**
- \`SchedulingService.SplitBookingAsync\` (~L2671) only redistributes UNPAID pay-at-studio bookings; it explicitly REFUSES package-credit bookings (\`BOOKING.CREDIT_BOOKING\`, L2687-2689) and already-paid ones. It creates SEPARATE single-seat PAY_AT_STUDIO attendances (Quantity=1, own AmountDueAtStudio) — so split-bill seats are each valued by their own payer, but it never touches credit bookings.
- The mis-attribution lives in the CREDIT multi-seat path, which split-bill does not intercept: \`DeductCreditAsync\` (WalletService L119-142) walks the client's active packages in expiry order and SPANS multiple ClientPackages when the first lacks enough credits — but the attendance stores only ONE \`PackageInstanceId = packages.First().Id\` (\`SettleBookingWithCreditAsync\` L1403/1416; same single-stamp on the qty-stepper \`AdjustAttendeeQuantityAsync\` L2810 which deducts \`delta\` across packages without re-stamping). \`PayrollService\` (L713-714) then values ALL seats at \`packages.First().FractionalValuePerClass * qty\`.
- Verdict: a single attendance with Quantity>1 whose credits actually drew from TWO packages (e.g. a nearly-empty older package + a fresh one; for MAT even a MAT wallet spilling into a GROUP wallet with a different per-class value) is commission-valued entirely at the first (earliest-expiry) package's rate. The "both seats valued by the first package" mis-attribution is real and reachable. Not fixed here (out of scope for this card) — flagging for a follow-up.

**Branch / tip:** \`feature/notes-commission\` off \`origin/feature/client-notes\`, tip \`1134338\` (pushed, remote verified). dotnet build (SoulPilates.API, Release, sdk 10.0) = 0 errors; astro build (node:22-alpine) = 62 pages OK.

**Prod deploy (superset — ships client-notes + this fix; the 5 Ideas features are already on prod):**
\`\`\`
cd /opt/soulpilates && git fetch origin && git checkout -B main origin/feature/notes-commission && scripts/deploy-prod.sh
\`\`\``;

async function main() {
  const board = await prisma.board.findUnique({ where: { id: BOARD_ID } });
  const col = await prisma.boardColumn.findUnique({ where: { id: COL_ID } });
  if (!board) throw new Error('board not found: ' + BOARD_ID);
  if (!col) throw new Error('column not found: ' + COL_ID);
  console.log('board:', board.name, '| column:', col.name);

  const minPos = await prisma.card.aggregate({ where: { columnId: COL_ID }, _min: { position: true } });
  const pos = (minPos._min.position ?? 0) - 1;

  const card = await prisma.card.create({
    data: {
      boardId: BOARD_ID,
      columnId: COL_ID,
      title: 'Commission: free private = group-credit rate (+ split-bill verify)',
      type: 'FEATURE',
      priority: 'HIGH',
      assignee: 'claude',
      position: pos,
      description: 'Bundled free-private class now pays the instructor the parent package\'s group per-class commission rate (was 0 → private drop-in fall-through). Read-only verify of split-bill / multi-package credit mis-attribution. See Claude comment for files/lines, verdict, branch tip, deploy note.',
      comments: { create: [{ authorName: 'Claude', body: comment }] },
    },
    include: { comments: true },
  });
  console.log('card created:', card.id, '| comment:', card.comments[0].id);
}
main().then(() => prisma.$disconnect()).catch(async (e) => { console.error('ERR', e.message); await prisma.$disconnect(); process.exit(1); });
